{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' current_policy.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n\nMeals:\n\n- Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n- Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n\nRide-share:\n\n- Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n- Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n\nSupplies:\n\n- Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n\nTrip covered by this audit:\n\n- Employee: Jordan Lee\n- Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n- Covered lodging nights: 2\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
